WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.558
Some things happen again and
again, in the same order.

2
00:00:07.778 --> 00:00:13.397
That is a pattern. Spot the part that
repeats, and you can say what comes next.

3
00:00:13.897 --> 00:00:18.402
Look at these beads. Orange,
teal, orange, teal, orange.

4
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:23.266
Say the colours out loud, and let
your voice run on past the end.

5
00:00:23.486 --> 00:00:27.201
Your voice wants to say teal
next. Your voice is right.

6
00:00:27.421 --> 00:00:34.898
Two colours can take turns, and that is a pattern
too. It repeats the same part over and over.

7
00:00:35.118 --> 00:00:40.180
So start at the beginning every
time, and let the words carry you on.

8
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.884
Every pattern has one
small part that repeats.

9
00:00:44.104 --> 00:00:47.680
Purple, gold, gold. Then
purple, gold, gold again.

10
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.476
Three beads repeat. You can
draw a line after every three.

11
00:00:51.696 --> 00:00:55.365
Now one bead is missing. Look
at the bead before the hole.

12
00:00:55.585 --> 00:00:59.207
The part that repeats tells
you exactly what belongs there.

13
00:00:59.707 --> 00:01:03.190
Numbers make patterns too.
Two, four, six, eight, ten.

14
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.103
Each number is two more
than the one before it.

15
00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:10.317
That is a jump pattern, and the
jump is the same every time.

16
00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:14.252
A jump can go backwards too.
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six.

17
00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:18.281
Find the jump first. Then you
can fill any hole in the line.

18
00:01:18.781 --> 00:01:22.681
Some patterns grow. Each one
adds a new row of two shapes.

19
00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:26.617
Two shapes, then four, then
six. Count them every time.

20
00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:30.041
The counts jump up by two,
just like the numbers did.

21
00:01:30.261 --> 00:01:33.930
So pattern four has eight
shapes. Six, and two more.

22
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.911
A growing pattern gets bigger
by the same amount each time.

23
00:01:38.411 --> 00:01:41.569
The equals sign means the
same amount on both sides.

24
00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:44.111
It does not mean here comes the answer.

25
00:01:44.331 --> 00:01:47.768
Three add something makes
seven. How many are missing?

26
00:01:47.988 --> 00:01:51.703
Count on from three: four,
five, six, seven. That is four.

27
00:01:51.923 --> 00:01:56.335
Now a scale. Four add two on
one side, three on the other.

28
00:01:56.555 --> 00:02:00.363
Add three more, and it sits
level. Both sides make six.

29
00:02:00.863 --> 00:02:05.043
A pattern has a part that
repeats. Find it and carry on.

30
00:02:05.263 --> 00:02:08.420
A jump pattern goes up or
down by the same amount.

31
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.031
And equals means the same on
both sides. Now go and try it.
